    `A move from one menu screen to another, a link's, a redirect's or the browser's Back or Forward, cross-fades the page in the browser's view transition ([[R2117000]]). No move into or out of a board's route fades, nor one off a board on screen, a replay in place among them: the animation queue owns what moves there. A change of query alone, Reduce motion and a browser without the API draw the move at once, and a move the leave guard holds ([[R1754000]]) fades once it goes. Presentation only (CLAUDE.md rule 7).`

11. **Add a paragraph to `apps/web/README.md`**, after the paragraph ending "fails when the page is taller or wider than its allowance.":

    `A move between two menus cross-fades (R2117000): \`net/navigate.ts\`'s \`showMove\` runs it inside \`document.startViewTransition\`, the render flushed with \`flushSync\`. A move into or out of a board's route (\`isBoardPath\`), off a board on screen, within one screen, under Reduce motion (\`settings/motion.ts\`) or without the API is drawn at once; a move the leave guard holds (R1754000) waits for it.`

