## Tests

**File:** `apps/web/src/net/viewTransition.test.tsx` (new).
- Header comment cites R2117000.
- Copy `traverse`, `guard()` and `releases` from `apps/web/src/net/navigate.test.tsx`.
- Import:
  - `at` from `../test/stubServer.ts`;
  - `setReducedMotion` from `../test/setup.ts`;
  - `writeSettings` and `__resetSettingsForTests` from `../settings/store.ts`;
  - `setFxSettings` and `resetFxSettingsForTests` from `../fx/settings.ts`;
  - `testid` from `../game/contract.ts`;
  - `guardLeaving`, `navigate`, `paths`, `usePathname` and `useSearch` from `./navigate.ts`.

Add this stub and screen:
```tsx
const drawnInside: string[] = [];
const start = vi.fn((update: () => void) => {
  update();
  drawnInside.push(document.querySelector('[data-testid="shown"]')?.textContent ?? "");
});
function Screen(): ReactElement {
  const path = usePathname();
  const search = useSearch();
  return <p data-testid="shown">{path + search}</p>;
}
```
`Screen` holds two readers, which proves that one move starts one transition. `drawnInside` proves `flushSync` works: the new screen is drawn by the time the update returns.

**`beforeEach`:**
- `start.mockClear()`
- `drawnInside.length = 0`
- `Object.defineProperty(document, "startViewTransition", { configurable: true, writable: true, value: start })`
- `at(paths.decks)`

**`afterEach`:**
- release every guard
- `cleanup()`
- `document.body.replaceChildren()`
- `Reflect.deleteProperty(document, "startViewTransition")`
- `setReducedMotion(false)`, `__resetSettingsForTests()` and `resetFxSettingsForTests()`
- `window.localStorage.clear()`

Wrap every `navigate` in `act`. All tests go in `describe("R2117000 a move between two menu screens cross-fades in a view transition", …)`:

1. `it("R2117000 a navigate from one menu screen to another starts one view transition, and the new screen is drawn inside it")`
   - Render `<Screen />`, then `navigate(paths.collection)`.
   - Expect: `start` called once, `drawnInside` equals `[paths.collection]`, the pathname is `paths.collection`.

2. `it("R2117000 the browser's Back and Forward between two menu screens each start one view transition")`
   - Navigate to `paths.collection`, then `mockClear()` and empty `drawnInside`.
   - `await traverse(() => window.history.back())`. Expect one call, with `drawnInside` equal to `[paths.decks]`.
   - Traverse forward. Expect two calls in total, the last one drawn being `paths.collection`.

3. `it("R2117000 no move into or out of a board route starts a view transition")`
   - Call `at(paths.play)`, then render.
   - For each of `paths.match("m-1")`, `paths.watch("m-1")`, `paths.duos("m-1")`, `paths.practice`, `paths.hotseat` and `paths.duosDev`: navigate to it, then back to `paths.play`. Check the pathname and the `shown` text after each move.
   - Then navigate to `paths.match("m-1")` and traverse Back and Forward.
   - Expect `start` never called.

4. `it("R2117000 a move off a board on screen, as a replay playing in place, starts no view transition")`
   - At `paths.replays`, render `<><Screen /><div data-testid={testid.board} /></>`.
   - Navigate to `paths.play`.
   - Expect no call, and the screen shows `/play`.

5. `it("R2117000 under Reduce motion, the system's, the settings panel's or the effects setting's, a move starts no view transition and still happens")`
   - Make three moves, each under one source of Reduce motion:
     - decks→collection under `setReducedMotion(true)`;
     - collection→decks under `writeSettings({ reduceMotion: true })`;
     - decks→collection under `setFxSettings({ motion: "reduce" })`.
   - Undo each source before setting the next.
   - After each move, expect the `shown` text to be the new path.
   - Expect no call at all.

6. `it("R2117000 where the browser has no view transitions a move happens at once")`
   - Define `startViewTransition` with `value: undefined` (configurable, writable).
   - Navigate to `paths.collection`.
   - Expect no throw, and the screen shows `/collection`.

7. `it("R2117000 a move the leave guard holds starts no view transition until it is let go")`
   - **Held navigate:**
     - At `paths.creator`, render, then call `guard()`.
     - Expect `navigate(paths.decks)` to return `false`, no call, and the pathname still `paths.creator`.
     - Run `act(() => held[0]?.())`. Expect one call and the pathname `paths.decks`.
   - **Held Back:**
     - Release the guards. Navigate to `paths.creator` (call 2), then call `guard()` again; name its array `held2`.
     - `traverse(back)`. Expect still 2 calls and the pathname `paths.creator`.
     - `traverse(() => held2[0]?.())`. Expect 3 calls, the last one drawn being `paths.decks`.

8. `it("R2117000 a change of the query alone stays on its screen and starts no view transition")`
   - At `paths.almanac`, navigate to `paths.almanacCard("core-001")`.
   - Expect no call, and the `shown` text ends with `?card=core-001`.

**Commands.** Run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` if needed, then `sh scripts/build-wasm.sh` (the vitest setup loads its module). Then:
- `pnpm --dir apps/web exec vitest run src/net/viewTransition.test.tsx src/net/navigate.test.ts src/net/navigate.test.tsx src/routes/creator.test.tsx src/together/ChallengeToast.test.tsx src/economy/JlorePill.test.tsx src/game/useOsReducedMotion.test.tsx src/static-pages.test.ts`
- `pnpm --dir apps/web test`: the full suite, because navigate.ts and animations.ts are imported almost everywhere.

## Done when

- [ ] A menu-to-menu `navigate` and a menu-to-menu `popstate` each start exactly one transition, flushed inside it (tests 1–2).
- [ ] No transition into or out of a board route, or off a board on screen (tests 3–4).
- [ ] Reduce motion (all three sources) and a missing API start none, and the move still happens (tests 5–6).
- [ ] A held `navigate` and a held Back start nothing until released (test 7).
- [ ] The R2117000 note, the 11-rulings entry, the §10.10 paragraph and the README paragraph are in, and `spec/INDEX.md` is regenerated.
- [ ] These checks are green: `pnpm --dir apps/web typecheck`, `pnpm --dir apps/web test`, `pnpm exec eslint apps/web e2e`, `cargo jackioh spec check`, `cargo fmt --check`, and the harness's web-test command.
- [ ] No `.skip`, `.only`, `eslint-disable` or `@ts-*` was added.
- [ ] The PR says `Part of #2036`, closes #2117, and carries one `## Player note` line, e.g. "Menus now fade into one another instead of cutting; games, replays and Reduce motion stay as they were."

## Risks

- **Config loading.** If any new navigate.ts import reaches `@jackioh/*`, `game/animations.ts` or the catalog, the Vite and vitest configs break. Every vitest run loads them, so a green run proves they still load.
- **R1754000.** With one `popstate` listener, `heldPop` runs once per pop instead of once per reader. The behaviour should not change; `navigate.test.tsx`, `creator.test.tsx` and `ChallengeToast.test.tsx` must stay green.
- **Address timing.** `go` must still change the address synchronously; only the render waits for the browser's capture. Callers read `window.location` right after `navigate`, so never move `pushState` into the callback.
- **#1756.** `navigate.test.ts` must pass unchanged. jsdom has no `startViewTransition`, so it exercises the immediate path.
- **e2e smoke in Chrome.** For the fade's ~250 ms after a menu move, clicks land on `<html>`. Cypress retries actionability, but if the smoke job flakes, first suspect a spec that clicks right after a menu move.
- **Rule 7.** This is presentation only: it reads the address and the DOM, never game state.

## Open questions

- `/practice` counts as a board route, so its setup screen (a menu under R1581000) does not fade: a practice link can start a game directly. A person may prefer the setup to fade.
- The Conquest series screen (`/series/:id`) fades as a menu; moving from it into its match does not fade.
